00:10:52,660 --> 00:10:54,940
Which does sound like a political party.

219
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:57,560
It does sound like it, Hannah, but it is not.

220
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:59,940
Even though it shares the same three dimensions

221
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:01,360
that Ruth talked about, I mean,

222
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,660
it has people in government who are members,

223
00:11:03,660 --> 00:11:07,600
it is an organization, and people recognize it as a brand,

224
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,460
it is not a party.

225
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:10,900
So, you know, if we're thinking about like,

226
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:14,420
what is the DSA, the DSA, and I think its current incarnation

227
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:16,800
is doing some of all of these things, right?

228
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:19,940
Like there are individuals who are getting elected

229
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:23,060
to hire office who presumably would try and work

230
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:26,420
with other DSA members to advance a shared agenda.

231
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:28,740
That's sort of the parties in government dimension.

232
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:31,500
They're a live and well organization

233
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:33,300
that are helping to get candidates elected

234
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:36,240
and distributing resources and sharing information

