00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:11,760
But tonight, because of what we did on this day, in this election, at this defining moment,

282
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:14,240
change has come to America.

283
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:19,440
Barack Obama had won the presidency.

284
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:22,400
The Democratic Party had a unified government,

285
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:26,400
which means they controlled the House, the Senate, and the presidency.

286
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:29,880
And after this election, Republicans were nursing their losses,

287
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:32,000
trying to figure out what went wrong,

288
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:35,880
and many of them were pretty unhappy with their own party.

289
00:14:35,880 --> 00:14:38,920
George W. Bush had left office deeply unpopular,

290
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:43,720
and some on the right felt like their team had lost the plot.

291
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:49,420
And that kind of a situation is ripe for an intraparty movement to gather steam.

