00:22:15,620 --> 00:22:19,380
So most members of the DSA are running as Democrats.

441
00:22:19,380 --> 00:22:21,780
There are like a scant few independents

442
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:22,860
and Green Party members,

443
00:22:22,860 --> 00:22:26,100
but it is a capital D democratic movement.

444
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:27,980
And I wanna resay here, Hannah,

445
00:22:27,980 --> 00:22:29,820
just because you believe in the tenets

446
00:22:29,820 --> 00:22:31,260
of democratic socialism,

447
00:22:31,260 --> 00:22:34,100
doesn't make you a member of this club.

448
00:22:34,100 --> 00:22:37,140
Now the DSA is obviously in support

449
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:38,620
of this political philosophy,

450
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:43,620
which is unchecked capitalism is an obstacle to life, liberty,

451
00:22:43,620 --> 00:22:45,020
and the pursuit of happiness.

452
00:22:45,020 --> 00:22:47,160
The word democratic at the beginning

453
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,900
means that the people, not the state,

454
00:22:49,900 --> 00:22:51,440
dictate their government.

455
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:54,180
This is in direct opposition to what we call authoritarian

456
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:58,340
socialism, like we saw in, say, Stalinist Russia.

457
00:22:58,340 --> 00:23:00,780
And socialism, it's kind of a tough word

458
00:23:00,780 --> 00:23:02,880
to define in one sentence, but I'll give it a whack.

459
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:05,620
This is a quote from labor journalist Sarah Jaffe.

460
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:08,540
She said it is quote that the people who do the work

461
00:23:08,540 --> 00:23:12,340
are the ones who make the decisions about what gets produced and how.

462
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:16,860
And how did this inter-party movement, the DSA, actually start?

463
00:23:16,860 --> 00:23:21,220
Well, the club started in the United States in the 1980s, but it didn't really grow in

464
00:23:21,220 --> 00:23:26,860
popularity until Bernie Sanders, a self-described Democratic socialist, ran against Hillary

465
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:30,900
Clinton for the Democratic nomination in the 2016 presidential election.

466
00:23:30,900 --> 00:23:36,780
Today, with your support and the support of millions of people throughout our country,

467
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:45,860
We begin a political revolution to transform our country economically, politically, socially,

468
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:48,820
and environmentally.

469
00:23:48,820 --> 00:23:56,060
And back then, there were around 6,000 members of the DSA, and today there are over 120,000.

470
00:23:56,060 --> 00:24:00,800
You said Bernie self-describes as a Democratic Socialist.

471
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:02,660
Is he a member of the DSA?

472
00:24:02,660 --> 00:24:04,500
He's not, ironically enough.

473
00:24:04,500 --> 00:24:10,260
He is not a member of the DSA, and anyone out there can say they're ideologically a democratic

474
00:24:10,260 --> 00:24:15,700
socialist, but that is a far cry from being endorsed by the DSA.

475
00:24:15,700 --> 00:24:21,080
So if a candidate is running for office and they want that endorsement, the DSA requires

476
00:24:21,080 --> 00:24:24,420
they fill out a submission form to be evaluated.

477
00:24:24,420 --> 00:24:30,860
This form is over 100 pages long, and the candidate has to prove their ideals are aligned

478
00:24:30,860 --> 00:24:32,060
with the movement.

479
00:24:32,060 --> 00:24:35,100
And what are those ideals exactly?

480
00:24:35,100 --> 00:24:41,420
Well, there are a lot, but the big one is shifting power from the wealthy to the workers.

481
00:24:41,420 --> 00:24:46,980
They advocate for unions, for Medicare for All, for tuition-free college opportunities

482
00:24:46,980 --> 00:24:53,100
for affordable housing, and increasing taxes on the wealthiest Americans.

483
00:24:53,100 --> 00:24:57,700
And another one, Hannah, and this one is big, especially as we are leading up to the midterms.

484
00:24:57,700 --> 00:25:05,340
The DSA has very strict rules about fundraising, i.e. no money from companies, no dark money

485
00:25:05,340 --> 00:25:08,120
from mysterious super PACs.

486
00:25:08,120 --> 00:25:13,620
If you are found to be taking that money, you are immediately expelled from the DSA.

487
00:25:13,620 --> 00:25:19,300
I say this, I'm bringing this up because a ton of money from wealthy individuals has

488
00:25:19,300 --> 00:25:21,640
already poured into the midterms.

489
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:24,700
a group of 20 people, 20 individuals,

490
00:25:24,700 --> 00:25:26,880
have given over a billion dollars.

491
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:32,160
All right, so there are some big DSA names out there,

492
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:34,960
the most recognizable ones in government right now,

493
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:37,120
being Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez,

494
00:25:37,120 --> 00:25:38,800
a US rep from New York,

495
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:41,620
Rashida Tlaib, who is a US rep from Michigan,

496
00:25:41,620 --> 00:25:45,360
and Zoran Mamdani, the current mayor of New York City.

497
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:50,360
Now, can we talk about the division

498
00:25:50,360 --> 00:25:52,680
that intro parties can create,

499
